#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.div:3117-6
msgctxt "user_guide/en.html:L1-formattingyourbook"
msgid "5 FORMATTING YOUR E-BOOK"
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.p:3119-6
msgid ""
"After learning the basics of KOReader from the previous section, now you "
"want to start reading probably. But before that, why not customize the "
"appearance of your book to make it look really nice."
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.p:3121-6
msgid ""
"In this section, we will do a step-by-step \"digital typesetting\" to make "
"your e-book look more like a printed book. Aim of this tutorial is to get "
"you familiar with the KOReader's <b>text appearance settings</b> so you can "
"change them according to your taste later."
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.p:3124-6
msgid "Here are the steps:"
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ol.li:3127-7
msgid ""
"<b>Get a nice font:</b> First we need a font for our book which looks more "
"like a printed book (and at the same time readable on an e-ink screen). If "
"you have a favorite font, you can use that. Otherwise you can download one "
"of our suggestions below. We have two fonts for different looks: <b>serif</"
"b> and <b>sans-serif</b> (if you don't know what these mean, just click on "
"the links to see the difference):"
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ol.li.ul.li:3133-8
msgid ""
"If you like <b>serif</b> fonts, download <b>Lusitana</b>. This is an elegant "
"classical serif typeface that is designed for reading long texts. You can "
"download it from <a href=\"https://fonts.google.com/specimen/"
"Lusitana\">here</a>."
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ol.li.ul.li:3136-8
msgid ""
"If you like <b>sans-serif</b> fonts, download <b>Red Hat Text</b>. This is a "
"geometric sans typeface that prioritizes legibility. You can download it "
"from <a href=\"https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Red+Hat+Text\">here</a>."
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ol.li:3140-7
msgid ""
"<b>Transfer the font to your device:</b> If you don't know how, check this "
"part of the guide and come back here after copying the font to your device: "
"<a href=\"#L2-fonts\" class=\"internalink\">Using your own fonts</a>. You "
"should restart KOReader after transferring the font so it can add the font "
"to the <span class=\"ui\">font list</span>."
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ol.li:3143-7
msgid ""
"<b>Set your new font:</b> Open your book and go to the menu you see below. "
"Your newly added font should appear at the beginning of the font list. "
"Select it:"
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ol.li.div:3145-7
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"TOP MENU / <img class=\"img_inline\" src=\"pictures/top_document.svg\" "
"style=\"width:26px;\"> / Font"
msgstr ""
